<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Santamaría</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a>–<a href="/years/1856">1856</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Santamaría was a drummer boy of humble origins from Alajuela and is the national hero of Costa Rica. During the Second Battle of Rivas in Nicaragua on 11 April 1856, in the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a>'s filibusters, he is said to have set fire to the building where the enemy was holding out and to have been killed doing so. Costa Rica's main international airport bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-santamaria.jpg" alt="Juan Santamaría" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manunuezp · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_Santamar%C3%ADa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
